To achieve a continuously running 1-minute countdown timer that generates a number and displays it in a table, with an additional button that, when clicked, causes the button's value to be displayed instead of the generated number, you can modify the previous example as follows:

### HTML

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>1 Minute Countdown</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div id="countdown">60</div>
    <table id="results-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Count</th>
                <th>Generated Number</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <!-- Generated numbers will appear here -->
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <button id="override-button">Override Value</button>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

